title: Arms for the Workers
subtitle: The civil guards' depots are full of rifles.
view-if: crisis_kapp = 1 or crisis_ruhr = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Arms for the Workers

Every town has its depot: rifles of the civil guards, the police armouries, the army's stores. In the Ruhr and in Thuringia the workers have already helped themselves. Elsewhere they are waiting for a word.

- @seize: Seize the depots.
- @battalions: Form workers' battalions under party discipline.
- @hide: Hide what we have for later.

@seize
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Arms us quickly, and alarms everyone else.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.kapp_armed = 1;
Q.red_guards_arms += 10;
Q.red_guards_strength += 4;
Q.civil_guards_strength -= 20;
Q.crisis_momentum += 6;
Q.repression += 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 5;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

In a dozen towns, armed workers walk into the depots and walk out with the rifles. In some, the civil guards fire first.

@battalions
subtitle: Fewer guns, more discipline.
on-arrival: {!
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 10;
Q.red_guards_strength += 2;
Q.crisis_momentum += 4;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Our battalions elect their officers and take their orders from the district leadership, not from whoever shouts loudest.

@hide
subtitle: Nothing now, something for the next time.
on-arrival: {!
Q.red_guards_arms += 4;
Q.repression -= 2;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 2;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Rifles go into allotment sheds and under the floorboards of union halls. The police will not find most of them.
